---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PlatformIcon from "../../components/PlatformIcon.astro";

const toc = [
  { label: "Install Modesto", href: "#install" },
  { label: "First chat", href: "#chat" },
  { label: "Add a project", href: "#project" },
  { label: "Choose an agent", href: "#agent" },
  { label: "Run the first task", href: "#first-task" },
  { label: "Review and ship", href: "#review" },
  { label: "Troubleshooting", href: "#troubleshooting" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Install Modesto, send a chat (even with no folder open), then open a Git repository and complete a first agent run."
  currentPath="/docs/get-started"
  eyebrow="Start here"
  {toc}
>
  <section id="install">
    <h2>Install Modesto</h2>
    <p>
      If the desktop app is not on this machine yet, follow the{" "}
      <a href="/docs/install">install guide</a>. You need a signed-in provider
      CLI before the first thread can run.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-card-grid">
      <article class="docs-card">
        <span class="platform-kicker"><PlatformIcon platform="macos" />macOS</span>
        <h3>Signed DMG</h3>
        <p>Apple silicon or Intel from the latest GitHub release.</p>
        <a href="/download">Download →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="docs-card">
        <span class="platform-kicker"><PlatformIcon platform="windows" /><PlatformIcon platform="linux" />Windows + Linux</span>
        <h3>Installer or AppImage</h3>
        <p>Windows x64 installer or Linux AppImage from Releases.</p>
        <a href="/download">Download →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="chat">
    <h2>Send a chat without a folder</h2>
    <p>
      Launch the desktop app. The first screen is a composer, not an empty
      project list. You can pick a provider and send immediately — chats no
      longer require opening a repository. Work still does. When you are ready
      to ship a change, add a project below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Details: <a href="/docs/threads">Threads and tasks</a>. On desktop, pop
      the thread out with the header control. See{" "}
      <a href="/docs/desktop">Desktop &amp; environments</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="project">
    <h2>Add a project</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <strong>Projects</strong> and choose an existing Git repository.</li>
      <li>Confirm the repository root and default branch.</li>
      <li>
        For the first run, prefer the current checkout if you are the only one
        editing. Use an isolated worktree when another person or agent may touch
        the same tree at the same time.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>Worktrees keep parallel tasks predictable.</strong>
      <p>
        Each thread can own a branch and a worktree so two agents do not fight
        over uncommitted files. See <a href="/docs/source-control">Source control</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="agent">
    <h2>Choose an agent</h2>
    <p>
      Use the provider and model pickers in the composer. Modesto only presents
      agents that were discovered and enabled in your provider settings.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirm the provider CLI is installed and signed in. Meta is <code>muse</code>; Copilot is <code>copilot</code>.</li>
      <li>Select a model and, if you want a read-only plan first, Plan mode.</li>
      <li>
        Review the <a href="/docs/permissions">permission mode</a> before sending.
        Full access is the product default; switch to Supervised if you want every
        command and file change to ask first.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/docs/providers">Read the provider guide →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="first-task">
    <h2>Run the first task</h2>
    <p>
      Describe the outcome, not every keystroke. Include acceptance criteria,
      constraints, and the checks you expect the agent to run.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-code">
      <div class="docs-code-head"><span>Example prompt</span><span>Composer</span></div>
      <pre><code>Fix the session reconnect bug.

Preserve the existing protocol and add focused regression coverage.
Show me the diff and call out any checks you could not run.</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>
      When the run reaches a safe seam — a coherent change, a blocked check, or
      a provider switch — create a <a href="/docs/checkpoints">checkpoint</a>{" "}
      before handing the thread to someone else.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="review">
    <h2>Review and ship</h2>
    <p>
      A completed run is not the same as an accepted change. Read the final
      response, open the changed-file list, inspect the diff, and confirm every
      reported check.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong>Continue</strong><span>Send a focused follow-up in the same thread when the objective and provider still fit.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Handoff</strong><span>Checkpoint and switch provider when another agent is better suited to the next step.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Review</strong><span>Open <a href="/docs/code-review">Code Review</a> when the implementation is coherent enough to inspect as a change.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Ship</strong><span>Commit, push, and open a pull request from the thread. See <a href="/docs/source-control">Source control</a>.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting">
    <h2>Troubleshooting the first run</h2>
    <div class="docs-table">
      <div><strong>No project open</strong><span>That is expected. Send an unscoped chat, or add a folder when you need a diff. Work still requires a project.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Provider missing</strong><span>Install the CLI, put it on <code>PATH</code> or set Binary path, sign in, and enable the instance in settings.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Run cannot edit</strong><span>Check the permission mode and confirm the selected project path is writable.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Unexpected Git state</strong><span>Stop the run, inspect the active checkout or worktree, and reconcile existing changes before continuing.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Session interrupted</strong><span>Resume the durable thread. Modesto keeps the timeline even when the provider process restarts.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
